From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: explorer: desktop icons at Windows' sizes, drawn at their size

The desktop's View sizes were 24, 32 and 48 px -- a step below Windows 10's
Small 32, Medium 48 and Large 96 -- so on a 1920x1200 laptop the default
"Medium" icons looked small. They are Windows' now, Medium (48) by default,
and each icon is taken from its file at the size it is drawn
(PrivateExtractIcons) instead of the 32 px image stretched.

Gate: test/desktop-gate.sh (make test-desktop).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/desktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/desktop.c
@@ -69,7 +69,9 @@
 #define WM_SG_DESKTOP_RESCAN (WM_USER + 0x5344)
 #define SG_RESCAN_TIMER      0x5345
